Copy the four derived members as one contiguous tail block with `std::memcpy` instead of four separate assignments, reducing instruction count and letting the compiler emit a single wide move.

```cpp
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
{
    std::memcpy(reinterpret_cast<char*>(this) + sizeof(FieldBase),
                reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&field) + sizeof(FieldBase),
                sizeof(Field) - sizeof(FieldBase));
}
```